From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:09:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Trim the menus for a handheld console

The main menu has New Game, Load, Save, Options and Quit, one level
instead of a Single Player menu, its items cut out of sp_menu.lmp and
mainmenu.lmp: there is no network play and the help pages are about the
keyboard. Options has Reset to defaults,
Brightness, Sound Volume, Always Run and a Crosshair switch, without the
console, which needs a keyboard, the key bindings, the mouse settings,
screen size, CD music and video modes. Leaving the options writes
config.cfg right away, not only on quitting: a handheld is often just
switched off.
---
 WinQuake/menu.c     | 232 +++++++++++++++++---------------------------
 WinQuake/quakedef.h |   1 +
 2 files changed, 91 insertions(+), 142 deletions(-)

diff --git a/WinQuake/menu.c b/WinQuake/menu.c
index a2fa76f..2dfa5d5 100644
--- a/WinQuake/menu.c
+++ b/WinQuake/menu.c
